      "message": "Ah, ok, I think I\u0027ve found the issue here.\n\nhttps://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/3547569/1/sound/soc/intel/boards/Kconfig\n\n```\nconfig SND_SOC_INTEL_SOUNDWIRE_SOF_MACH\n...\n\tselect SND_SOC_RT721_SDCA_SDW\n```\n\n```\nbrya_device.fragment\n216:CONFIG_SND_SOC_INTEL_SOUNDWIRE_SOF_MACH\u003dm\n```\n\nIn the short term, I think we can fix the build errors by dropping that patch from this series. We may not need it at all in the `android16-6.12-desktop` branch, and just rely on setting `SND_SOC_RT721_SDCA_SDW\u003dm` explicitly in `private/google-modules/linux/brya` like any other module.\n\nI\u0027m not sure what the answer is in terms of cleanly landing that patch if we do need it though. Presumably there\u0027s a process which allows these types of patches, since this is unlikley to be the first, won\u0027t certainly won\u0027t be the last.",
